<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kilkenny Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1200</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny">Kilkenny</a> Castle is a castle above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-nore">River Nore</a> in Kilkenny, Ireland, first built for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-marshal-1st-earl-of-pembroke">William Marshal</a> in the early 13th century on the site of an earlier Norman fortification. James Butler, 3rd Earl of Ormond, bought it in 1391, and it became the main seat of the Butler earls and dukes of Ormond. The family kept it until 1967, when it was handed to the people of Kilkenny.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kilkenny-castle.jpg" alt="Kilkenny Castle" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Tolivero~commonswiki assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kilkenny-castle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
